{"description":"The terminal interface: message pane, device list showing presence and custom status, input line, and a status line carrying connection state.\n\nThe vision's hardest constraint applies here more than anywhere else — a working session must be reachable in no more than three commands, for a reader who is not technical. Discoverability is a requirement of this item, not a nicety.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. A new user reaches a working session in no more than three commands, with no configuration file to hand-edit.\n2. Presence and custom status are visible without issuing a command.\n3. Connection state is always on screen, including while degraded or reconnecting.\n4. The interface is usable at 80 columns and degrades legibly on a terminal without colour support.\n5. It runs over SSH on a headless device with no desktop environment present.\n6. Every command is discoverable from within the interface, without reading external documentation."}